  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to run",
      "items": [
        "cd rust && cargo run --release --bin states -- --state minus-x|neel|neel-x [--lmin 4 --lmax 8] [--gammas 0,0.01,0.1] [--dt 0.1] [--t-max 1000] [--stop 1e-3] [--seed 1] [--stop-te F] [--channel z|x|y|dep|decay|thermal] [--obs-dt Δ] [--op-ent-dt Δ′]",
        "Output in data/ (or $SCARS_DATA_DIR); suffix _ch<channel> for a channel other than σᶻ, _seed<N> for realization N ≠ 1",
        "Analysis order (default dir data/used_data): fit_states.py → fit_small_gamma.py → fit_states_inverse_L.py; fit_channels.py → plot_operator_spreading.py; plot_states.py any time",
        "Copy the figures from data/used_data/ into latex/figures/ before compiling the notes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Notes part",
      "items": [
        "Compile: latex/build_parts.sh exact_rho → latex/parts/pdf/exact_rho.pdf (full notes are built first; numbering as in latex/notes.tex)",
        "1 Model; 2 Theory: 2.4 Other single-site noise channels, 2.5 What the new observables measure",
        "3 How the simulations are done: 3.1 Notation, 3.2 Pauli strings, 3.4 Density matrices: exact evolution in the Pauli basis, 3.7 Operator entanglement, 3.8 Other single-site noise channels, 3.9 Operator observables of ρ, 3.12 Run options and file names",
        "4 How the decay rates are computed; 5 Exact results; 6 Scar against thermal decay up to L = 20; 7 Small γ: the finite-size cap",
        "10 Results of the lean runs: 10.1 Runs and checks, 10.2 Thermodynamic rates under every noise channel, 10.4 Operator spreading of the evolving state"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Key mechanics",
      "items": [
        "ρ = 2^−L Σ_P r_P P: the generator is real (antisymmetric H part plus diagonal channel damping); random c removes translation, so the full 4^L basis is used, matrix-free from L = 11",
        "One random-c realization per L from Rng(1000·seed + L); the γ list runs in parallel on the same 𝓛",
        "Each output step: exp(𝓛 dt) as a Taylor series summed to round-off in substeps of norm ≤ 4; output step min(dt, DT_GAMMA/γ)",
        "Stop when the signal (m_⊥, |s_z| or s_⊥) stays below --stop for STOP_WINDOW, at --stop-te × the first 1/e time, or at --t-max; γ = 0 runs to --t-zero and checks reference 1"
      ]
    }
  ]
